# Copy to .env and fill in. scripts/reset.sh sources .env automatically.
#
# NOTE: `jac run` / `jac start` do NOT read .env on their own -- only
# scripts/reset.sh does (it sources this file with `set -a`). To run anything
# else against the real model, export the key in your shell first:
#
#   export OPENAI_API_KEY=sk-...
#   jac run scripts/verify_llm.jac     # proves all 8 byLLM roles really fire
#
# There is no fallback in this app. With no key set, every model-backed action
# (building a plan, matching a pledge, escalating a need, ...) raises a clear
# error and the UI badge reads "NO MODEL CONNECTION" -- see core/reason.jac.

OPENAI_API_KEY=sk-...

# Optional: override the model set in jac.toml ([byllm.model] default_model)
# BYLLM_DEFAULT_MODEL=gpt-4o-mini
